**DBS GPT Web Search: What It Can Do and Where It Falls Short**

If you have been using DBS GPT to automate the retrieval of information from external websites, there is a good chance you have run into some unexpected behaviour. This article walks through how the web search feature actually works under the hood, and highlights two key limitations you should be aware of before building it into your workflows.

**How Web Search Works in DBS GPT**

The web search capability in DBS GPT is not a simple browser call. It is itself powered by an LLM, specifically Gemini 2.5 Flash as of April 2026. What this means in practice is that when a search step is executed, the LLM decides what keywords to use based on the instructions it has been given. It then conducts the search and attempts to extract the relevant information from the results.

This has an important implication: the quality and specificity of your search is directly tied to how clearly you describe what you want. The more explicit you are, the better the search will be. Vague instructions tend to produce vague searches.

