**What DBS GPT Web Search Does Well**

It is worth being clear that this is not a feature to avoid, it just has a sweet spot. DBS GPT handles web search reliably when:

- The target is a specific, stable URL that does not require any prior browser interaction to reach
- The file you want, whether a PDF or CSV, has its own unique download link that is directly accessible
- The content is text-based and indexable, meaning the LLM can find it through a well-formed search query

A good example of this working well would be a PDF report that lives at a permanent, predictable URL on a government or institutional website, where the link itself can be found through a straightforward text search. In that scenario, DBS GPT can locate the link, navigate to it, and retrieve the file without needing to interact with any page elements.

