**The Takeaway**

Web search in DBS GPT is genuinely useful, but it works best under certain conditions. To get the most out of it:

- Be as explicit as possible in your search instructions, since an LLM is deciding the keywords
- Always review AI-generated workflow steps rather than trusting them blindly
- Double-check that target websites are explicitly named in web search steps
- Avoid relying on it for pages that require JavaScript interactions to surface the data you need
- Do not expect it to browse and explore a site the way a human would — if retrieving the right file requires first scanning what is available, you will need to handle that logic yourself or hardcode the target URL
- For file downloads, it works best when the PDF or CSV has a unique, discoverable link rather than being tucked behind dynamic page interactions

When you design with these constraints in mind, the feature becomes a lot more predictable and reliable.

